What is your mywc program test plan?


Boundary tests:

mywcempty.txt: Empty file. Tests the boundary where the while loop
condition on line 30 is immediately false, so only lines 30, 52, 55,
56 execute.

mywcspaces.txt: Contains only spaces. Tests the boundary where every
character is whitespace but iInWord is never set TRUE, so lines 36
and 44 are both false. Executes lines 30, 32, 34, 36, 48, 52, 55, 56.

mywcnewlines.txt: Contains only newlines. Tests the boundary where
every character is whitespace and a newline. Executes lines 30, 32,
34, 36, 48, 49, 52, 55, 56.

mywcsinglechar.txt: Contains a single non-whitespace character with
no newline. Tests the boundary of a one-character file ending
mid-word. Executes lines 30, 32, 34, 44, 45, 48, 52, 53, 55, 56.

mywccharsonly.txt: Contains only non-whitespace characters with no
spaces or newlines. Tests boundary where isspace is never true and
iInWord is set once and never reset. Executes lines 30, 32, 34, 44,
45, 48, 52, 53, 55, 56.

mywcnonewline.txt: Contains words separated by a space but no
trailing newline. Tests the boundary where EOF is reached while
iInWord is TRUE. Executes lines 30, 32, 34, 36, 38, 39, 44, 45, 48,
52, 53, 55, 56.

Statement tests:

mywcmultiword.txt: Contains multiple words per line separated by
spaces, ending with newlines. Causes the computer to execute lines
30, 32, 34, 36, 38, 39, 44, 45, 48, 49, 52, 55, 56.

mywctabs.txt: Contains words separated by tab characters with
newlines. Tabs are whitespace per isspace(), exercising the same
paths as spaces. Causes the computer to execute lines 30, 32, 34,
36, 38, 39, 44, 45, 48, 49, 52, 55, 56.

mywcwordspace.txt: Contains words followed by spaces on one line.
Specifically exercises line 36 (iInWord TRUE mid-loop) and lines 38,
39. Causes the computer to execute lines 30, 32, 34, 36, 38, 39, 44,
45, 48, 52, 55, 56.

mywcmix.txt: Contains a mix of spaces, tabs, newlines, and words.
Exercises all branches collectively. Causes the computer to execute
lines 30, 32, 34, 36, 38, 39, 44, 45, 48, 49, 52, 55, 56.

Stress tests:

mywclargewords.txt: Contains 1000 lines each with one word. Stress
tests line and word counting with a large number of lines.

mywclargestandard.txt: Contains 500 lines each with 10 random words.
Stress tests general word and line counting with a large realistic
input.

mywclargestress.txt: Contains a single long line of nearly 50000
characters with no trailing newline. Stress tests character counting
and the EOF mid-word path with maximum input size.

